Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:02.480
- [Instructor] In this
video, we wanna compute

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:07.480
what 833 divided by seven is.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.850
So I encourage you to pause this video

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:13.580
and see if you can figure
that out on your own.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:14.900
All right, now let's
work through it together.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.410
And you might have appreciated,

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:17.750
this is a little bit more difficult

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.430
than things that we have done in the past.

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:21.770
And in this video, I'm
going to show you a method

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:24.350
that your parents have probably not seen,

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.220
but you'll see that it's kind of fun,

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.630
and it's called division
with partial quotients,

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:32.070
which is a very fancy word,
but as I said, it'll be fun.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:35.142
So, the first thing I will
do is I will rewrite this

00:00:35.142 --> 00:00:40.142
as 833 divided by, divided by seven.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.350
So you can view these
as the same expression.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.780
The reason why we do it
this way is it formats it

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:49.670
so it's a little bit easier

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.380
to do our division with partial quotients.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.450
So the way that division
with partial quotients works,

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:56.290
and once again, it's not the way

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.310
that your parents probably
learned how to do it,

00:00:58.310 --> 00:00:59.610
is you just say, hey,

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.490
how many times can seven go into 833?

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:04.090
I don't have to get it exactly.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.750
I just wanna go under 833.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.230
And so my brain immediately thinks, well,

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:12.760
seven hundreds is less than 833,

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.220
so we're going to go into
833 at least 100 times.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:17.610
And so what we would do

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.403
is we would write that hundred up here.

00:01:20.403 --> 00:01:23.020
We'd wanna be very careful
about our place value.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:25.110
You can view this column
as the hundreds column,

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.550
this is the tens column,
this is the ones column,

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.960
and then we wanna see, how
much do we have left over?

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:33.860
How close did seven times 100 get us?

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:38.363
So what we do is we multiply
100 times seven to get 700,

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.980
and then we can subtract that
700 from 833 to figure out

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:44.820
how much more we have left.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:49.017
And so 833 minus 700 is 133.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.150
And so we can then say, all right,

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.920
we still have another 133 to go.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:00.730
So how many more times
can seven go into this?

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:03.750
Well, seven goes into 133,

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.790
once again, you don't
have to have it exactly.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:10.790
If you know seven times 10 is equal to 70,

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.080
actually, let's go with that.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.880
We know we go at least 10 times.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:15.410
So let's write that up here.

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:17.040
We're going at least 10 times,

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.820
and to figure out how
much more we have left,

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:22.560
let's multiply 10 times seven to get 70,

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.560
and then we can subtract,
and we see that we have,

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.670
let's see, three minus zero is three.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.980
13 tens minus seven tens is six tens.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.600
So we have 63 left.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.880
So seven definitely can go into 63.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:37.850
We're gonna keep doing this

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:41.890
until we have a number
less than seven over here.

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:44.610
So let's see, seven, how many
times does seven go into 63?

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:46.810
You might know from your
multiplication tables

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:49.290
that seven times nine is 63.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:50.870
So you could get it exactly.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.490
So you could just write that up here.

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:55.080
We have nine more times
to go into the number,

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.137
and then you would say
nine times seven is 63.

00:02:57.137 --> 00:02:59.940
You could say, hey, we got exactly there.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:01.560
We have nothing left over.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.570
And as long as this
number is less than seven,

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:06.650
you know that you can't
divide seven anymore

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.040
into our original number.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:10.800
And so, you're done.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.950
And so, how many times
does seven go into 833?

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:16.880
Well, we said it went 100 times,

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.690
and then we were able
to go another 10 times,

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.900
and then we were able to
go another nine times.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.450
And so what we wanna do
is add these numbers.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:28.450
So you wanna add 100 plus 10 plus nine.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.540
When you add up all of
them, what do you get?

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:35.300
You get nine ones, one 10, one hundred.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.760
You get 119, so this is equal to 119.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:41.580
All I did is I added these up.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.380
Now, I wanna be very clear
that you could do division

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:46.910
with partial quotients and
not do it exactly like this.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:48.660
That's kind of why it's fun.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.550
So let's do it another way.

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:52.870
So let's say we wanna figure out again

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:57.243
how many times does
seven go into 833, 833?

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:06.080
We could have said,
maybe it goes 150 times.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:08.280
So what you could have said
is you could have said,

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:12.800
all right, my current guess
or estimate is 150 times,

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:14.730
that I could multiply 150 times seven.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:15.563
How would I do that?

00:04:15.563 --> 00:04:17.990
Let's see, zero times seven is zero,

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:21.440
five times seven is 35.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:25.023
You can carry the three, so to speak.

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:31.770
One times seven is seven plus
that three is going to be 10.

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:34.090
And so that gets us to 1050.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:36.490
Well, over here, we just
finished overshooting.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:38.050
It doesn't go 150 times.

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:38.980
There's nothing left over.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:40.900
So 150 is too high.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:42.980
So we would wanna backtrack that.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:46.630
And then you would go, well
maybe I could go to 110.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:47.980
So let's try that out.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:51.810
So 110, and now let's multiply.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.960
Zero times seven is zero.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.940
One times seven is seven.

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.820
One times seven is seven.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:01.210
So, 110 times seven is 770.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.043
So that works.

00:05:02.043 --> 00:05:04.700
It's less than 833, but
let's see what we have left.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:07.750
So we subtract, we get a three here,

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:12.750
and then, let's see, 83 tens
minus 77 tens, that's six tens,

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:15.770
and actually, that got
us there a lot faster.

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:17.140
So then you could just know

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:19.640
that hey, seven goes into 63 times.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:20.980
But let's say we didn't know that.

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:21.880
We could say, all right,

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:25.790
let's say I'm gonna estimate
it goes eight times.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:28.310
So you would put an eight up here.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.080
And then you say, how much
did we have left over?

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:33.410
Eight times seven is 56.

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:38.410
You subtract, and then 63
minus 56 is exactly seven.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:42.690
And you say, okay, look,
I can go one more time.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:44.390
So I'd write that up there.

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:46.620
So one times seven is seven,

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.940
and then you see we
have nothing left over.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:50.100
So we are done.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.660
So how many times did it go in?

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:55.650
One plus eight is nine plus 110 is 119.

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:57.630
So hopefully, you find that interesting,

00:05:57.630 --> 00:06:00.500
and I really want you to think
about why this is working.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.720
We're just trying to see how many times

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:04.230
can we go in without overshooting it,

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.630
and then what's left over?

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:07.420
So how many more times can we go in,

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:08.620
and then what's left over,

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:10.210
and then how many more times can we go in,

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:12.520
until what we have left
over is less than seven,

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:15.523
so that we can't go
into it any more times.

